{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together","id":1104195,"title":"How do your coteries come together?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-16T01:15:33-07:00","id":1104195,"title":"How do your coteries come together?","content":"Whenever I run vampire my players have trouble finding reasons to join up as a coterie, let alone interact with each other; it often feels like I'm running a separate game for each person at the table. Does anyone have any tips to help me out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T01:35:44-07:00","id":1104199,"title":"","content":"They all learn something about the same problem and a higher up orders them together.<br /> They all feed in the same area and an outside threat requires them to work together.<br /> They all gain the same enemy and are advised to work together in a buddy system.<br /> Every day they dream of another member of the group, surely there must be a reason.<br /> Turns out their sires knew each other/are working together on something and have ordered them together.<br /> They're all kindred of interest in the same crime and need others who can collaborate their ongoing activities.<br /> The city has become more dangerous, everyone else is forming coteries and picking on the lone kindred too stupid to do the same.<br /> Yell at them for making your job hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 06-16-2017, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T03:53:02-07:00","id":1104216,"title":"","content":"I don't require my players to form coteries. I do tell them major storyline elements that may come up and that I'm not going to do a major detour for a few of them. (So it behooves them work together if they want to go elsewhere.) <br /> If their character wasn't present when an NPC said something, they don't know about it unless someone present tells them about it. This practice alone is sufficient for each player character to be on friendly terms with another player's character. It also empowers players who are participating in the main chronicle over those exclusively chasing private agendas.<br /> Inform your players before the game starts to come up with a reason to work together as a coterie or at least with one other player. Don't assume just because multiple characters share a covenant or interests that they'll work together.<br /> Be prepared for the possibility of that relationship going sour. Some players don't like having their characters kowtowing to another player, or insist on being the one in control. I had one player who's character was a total dick to every other player character except one. But the same player had another character that was extremely popular with the other characters during the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-16-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T06:34:02-07:00","id":1104259,"title":"","content":"Session 1, scene 1: someone with authority over all of the PCs informs them that they have been assigned some shared responsibility. &quot;The three of you are my deputies for enforcing [policy that will lead to interesting trouble.] You can pursue it how you want, here's a starting lead, check back in with my people once you've got something.&quot; Try to spend at least the first chapter or two with all of the PCs in the same scene as much as possible, don't spotlight their personal stuff until they've had some shared group experiences and built a rapport in-character.<br /> <br /> The cool thing about being the ST is that you pretty much have the authority to decide what happens onscreen. You can choose to create scenes with all/most of the PCs present at once, and gloss over solo stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T07:55:01-07:00","id":1104294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1104199#post1104199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turns out their sires knew each other/are working together on something and have ordered them together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one. My vampire's been too focused on the first tier of things, but I've always wanted to do one where the players are embraced by another, secret coterie. I figure it would fit well in a harsh domain where the Prince doesn't allow Embraces without express permission, and the sires doing it are doing it as part of a pact to move beyond their normal distrust and agree to have something on each other so they'll be less paranoid about working with one another.<br /> <br /> But usually it's just sort of chance. Either they live nearby each other, have been 'sent' to form a coterie by higher ups, or knew each other in life so gravitate towards each other in undeath.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:47:54-07:00","id":1104466,"title":"","content":"If there is no specific plot purpose for the coterie which should make the formation obvious then organically. After each player has a character concept, complete character is better, have each player share what they want the other players to know about their character and each person can figure out what they think about the other player characters in character. Basically, each player creates a relationship tree with the others. The coterie would be a web of shared interests and mutual acquaintances such that any one character may not have a strong connection to the rest but at least an indirect connection through someone in the coterie. The web could include mentors, allies, etc. but that might be a bit too complicated.<br /> <br /> I guess the short version would be to think of a coterie as a group of friends and figure out how they became a group of friends. There often is no one underlying tie that binds a group of friends. They didn't all decide to join the same club at school. It is a pair here and a trio there bound together by mutual acquaintances that creates a larger group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T06:43:56-07:00","id":1104712,"title":"","content":"You could also do what FATE and some other RPGs do - make &quot;how do you know the character next to you&quot; part of character creation. If need be, run a few prologues detailing these events/Scenes. If everyone knows someone else in the chain, that can be reason enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T10:35:24-07:00","id":1104773,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas everyone! I talked to some of my players and they weren't entirely sure why vampires would join together societal wise. They understood mages and their cabals, werewolves and their packs, and Hunters and their cells. So, is there any good way to explain why coteries are formed in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:01:35-07:00","id":1104785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1104773#post1104773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is there any good way to explain why coteries are formed in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>The snarky answer is &quot;have you tried setting an angry elder on them?&quot; But when you get down to it that's what it comes down to, there are things out there that you don't want to be fighting alown and there are times you need skills you don't prosess and having someone who plans to work with you in the future cuts the risk of betrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:14:30-07:00","id":1104814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1104785#post1104785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The snarky answer is &amp;quot;have you tried setting an angry elder on them?&amp;quot; But when you get down to it that's what it comes down to, there are things out there that you don't want to be fighting alown and there are times you need skills you don't prosess and having someone who plans to work with you in the future cuts the risk of betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. Do the Players' characters think they can accomplish everything on their own? Doubtful. Allies of convenience can turn into friends (or in this case, a Coterie) after long enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:50:18-07:00","id":1104829,"title":"","content":"I've run chronicles that basically ended up as three or four solo games, and while it's true to the personal side of the game it's not a good use of a session. These days I start with out-of-character agreement that the players will have characters who generally work together and sometimes pursue solo plotlines briefly or outside of regular sessions, and <i>then</i> come up with an in-character rationale like a shared interest, mutual enemy or external reason to work together.<br /> <br /> The last three in-character rationales were that the characters were refugees who had escaped an attack on their city's vampires, that the characters were all young outsiders at Elysium, and that the most experienced player's character had been asked to keep an eye on the new players' characters who were recently Embraced illegally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:19:23-07:00","id":1104839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1104785#post1104785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The snarky answer is &quot;have you tried setting an angry elder on them?&quot; But when you get down to it that's what it comes down to, there are things out there that you don't want to be fighting alown and there are times you need skills you don't prosess and having someone who plans to work with you in the future cuts the risk of betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games, I tend to consider that it is easier to lose your touch with humanity when you're a lone vampire. For me, a coterie is less a group of friends: it's an AA group for young-ish vampires (I tend to make newly embraced vampires lost and afraid, even if their sire takes care of them: it's a rather traumatizing experience. You're killed and then forced to live with your murderer to learn how to become a good member of his secret society of psychotic murderers). From there, it's easy to justify that vampiric society grows organically from those coteries and that older vampires, without the need for feeling humane, keep doing it because it gives them power and they have a lot of political capital invested in it.<br /> <br /> Basically, it gives weight to the option: they meet at a social gathering of vampires and they just latch on each other like a castaway on a floating board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T17:05:05-07:00","id":1104911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1104773#post1104773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the ideas everyone! I talked to some of my players and they weren't entirely sure why vampires would join together societal wise. They understood mages and their cabals, werewolves and their packs, and Hunters and their cells. So, is there any good way to explain why coteries are formed in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the players are at a loss, I can manufacture a reason for an encounter or rationale for one character to look up another. It's up to them to make it stick or generate in game rationale to not keep associating with them.<br /> <br /> For instance one of my player's belonged to the same bloodline as another PC. She was directed to get in touch with that PC to coordinate a project related to the bloodline's activities. Meeting was arranged, the other other PC was deliberately late and showed up drunk (He deliberately fed off some humans who were drunk.) and proceeded to call the other PC a whore (whom he didn't know) at an Invictus gathering and had to be escorted off and one of his retainers apologized for him.<br /> <br /> Another time a Sanctified PC was told to contact another Dragon PC about repairing their car. They hit it off well and got involved in a chop shop ring run by a pair of Carthians and eventually edged her out of business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-17-2017, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T21:16:51-07:00","id":1104972,"title":"","content":"After playing Mafia 3<br /> <br /> They were all screwed over by the same powerful elder and have banded together for revenge/profit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T08:27:53-07:00","id":1105703,"title":"","content":"In my last game I had them all granted the same hunting grounds, their sires didn't have much of a connection, but their sires all had connections to the Baron of the neighborhood their territory was in. That pretty quickly helped gel them together as they were dealing with similar issues having been recently embraced, and they had a shared resource they needed to work together to maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T15:38:26-07:00","id":1105858,"title":"","content":"In my current Chronicle there were three hooks:<br /> <br /> 1)- They were the new kids in town, the most recently Embraced so they banded together to climb up the political ladder<br /> 2)- I had them describe how they knew each other<br /> 3)- Rapidly I gave them a commun enemy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T05:18:11-07:00","id":1108714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1104195-how-do-your-coteries-come-together?p=1105703#post1105703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my last game I had them all granted the same hunting grounds, their sires didn't have much of a connection, but their sires all had connections to the Baron of the neighborhood their territory was in. That pretty quickly helped gel them together as they were dealing with similar issues having been recently embraced, and they had a shared resource they needed to work together to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Territory can be good, yeah. Especially in cities where the Prince's authority is not omniscient and omnipresent. How are you going to defend your hunting grounds when another coterie marches in? Best call your buddies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13616-nilaihah","name":"Nilaihah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}